    "what": "M1, L1 and K0 disallow Write, Edit, MultiEdit and NotebookEdit; M, L0 and K1 disallow Write, Edit and NotebookEdit only. No candidate disallows the shell tool, so in all six a reviewer that ignored the text could still change files through the shell; the frontmatter is therefore a partial guard everywhere, and the read-only obligation rests on the same instruction text in all six. Whether the intended host still offers a separate MultiEdit tool is UNVERIFIED (live host NOT_RUN); if it does not, the difference disappears.",
